1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,800
Cheap-Drive: an adaptive dispatcher for the Spread simulation.
Win the right work and deliver it reliably.

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:12,800
First, screen the request for pickup slack,
route length, and trade-ins. Illustrative Beta replay.

3
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,800
Price each viable option from its own list price,
with an adaptive markup and counted dealer trust.

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,800
Start the driver fee at 0.8 times the typical fee.
Increase it toward 1.5 times as the warning approaches.

5
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,800
Track the gig, driver booking, and delivery.
Timing and route are illustrative, not a live run.

6
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:34,800
Capture events, reconcile the ledger, and inspect failures.
The real report shown is a level-4 fixed-baseline tooling example.

7
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:39,000
1,022 completed practice worlds across 34 seed-and-level scenarios.
Repeated seeds are correlated, not independent validation weeks.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:48,800
The complete experiment chart includes failures.
Blue dots qualify; red crosses fail. Groups are not a time axis.

9
00:00:49,300 --> 00:01:00,800
Same stress seed: 500 km / 30% versus 600 km / 38% target.
More wins reduced margin and crossed below the 90% on-time gate.

10
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:09,500
Selective longer routes added 1,231.75 simulated euros per week.
Eight matched development seeds: higher margin and qualification on all eight.

11
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:15,800
Mean on-time fell from 96.35% to 95.51%; worst week was 92.98%.
This is a promising development result; unseen-week validation is still needed.

12
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:29,800
Five saved official ranking weeks totalled 50,541.26 simulated euros.
All five qualified. This historical ranking result is separate from the final.

13
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:40,000
Cheap-Drive. Win the right work. Deliver it reliably.
Next: validate on unseen weeks.
